      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here's the **Meridian Analytics Q3 2026 Business Report** for your review:\n\n---\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim, VP of Sales | Claire Fontaine, CFO\n\n### Executive Summary\nQ3 2026 was a strong quarter \u2014 the 15-person team closed **14 of 22 deals**, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals still pending, and all critical support issues were resolved same-day.\n\n### Sales Performance\n- **Total closed revenue:** $1,040,000\n- **Top region:** South \u2014 $468,000 in won deals\n- **Win rate:** 63.6% (above the 55% company target)\n- **Field sales team:** James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb worked 22 active opportunities\n- **Pending deals:** ~$240,000 across 3 deals expected to close by end of September\n- **Product mix:** Meridian Insights Pro drove the majority of closed revenue; Meridian DataBridge remains a strong land-and-expand vehicle\n\n### Key Highlights\n- **Top deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract (D019) on Sept 5\n- **Headcount:** 15 employees \u2014 Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), Finance (2)\n- **Support SLA:** All critical tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) resolved within 24 hours\n- **License utilization:** SKU-001 (Insights Pro) at **94% capacity** \u2014 procurement review scheduled for October\n\n### Next Steps\n1. Close pending deals (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target **$1.2M** in new ARR\n3. Resolve open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of customer success calls\n4. Conduct license capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi for Q4 roadmap\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you'd like to dive deeper into any section or cross-reference the data with the underlying sales or support records!",
        "status_code": null
      },
